        "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{1}\u27e82{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t=$",
        "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each componentt separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\u27e82{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(2{e}^{t}){|}_{0}^{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\,{|}_{0}^{1}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82{e}^{1}-2{e}^{0},\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u20611-\\operatorname{sin}\u20610\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82e-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u20611\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
